      "message": "fix(adaptive): read the bore's star cell through offset rounding noise\n\nThe Z 15 and Z 5 levels of the user's bore hand the planner a\n328-vertex disc outline. Its opening at the corner radius kept edges\none or two Clipper units long (1.4e-6 mm) that turn back about the\npole. The star law read each as a shadow, and the kernel test read its\nline as a wall through the area. The star cell was refused, and the\ngrowth rings cut those levels in 999.92 mm of feed against 334.31 mm.\n\nStar::new now drops the vertices of an opened row loop that stand\nwithin 1e-5 mm of the last vertex kept. Each bore level takes the morph\nspiral: Z 15 and Z 5 cut 330.07 mm and reach the wall in -Y. The bore\npin moves to (1642, 1614, 300), measured on macOS arm64 in release.\n\nFixes #4010\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
